The `condition` field of each `findings[]` record MUST match exactly ONE of the names below. Severity / extent / modifier values must come from the corresponding column. If a qualifier of that kind is not stated, leave the field null.

| Condition | Organs | Severity | Extent | Modifiers (key: allowed values) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
{% for c in schema.conditions -%}
| `{{ c.name }}` | {{ c.organs | join(', ') }} | {{ c.severity_values | join(', ') if c.severity_values else 'none' }} | {{ c.extent_values | join(', ') if c.extent_values else 'none' }} | {% if c.modifiers %}{% for k, vs in c.modifiers.items() %}`{{ k }}`: {{ vs | join(', ') }}{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% else %}none{% endif %} |
{% endfor %}

Condition descriptions and synonyms (use these to disambiguate):
{% for c in schema.conditions -%}
- `{{ c.name }}`: {{ c.description }}{% if c.synonyms %} _Synonyms_: {{ c.synonyms[:6] | join('; ') }}.{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

# Schema: negation_group values

The `negation_group` field of each `negations[]` record MUST match one of:
{% for n in schema.negation_flags %}
- `{{ n.name }}` ({{ n.organs | join(', ') }}): {{ n.description }}{% if n.synonyms %}  e.g. "{{ n.synonyms[0] }}"{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}

# Schema: quality flag values

The `flag` field of each `quality_flags[]` record MUST match one of:
{% for q in schema.quality_flags %}
- `{{ q.name }}` ({{ q.organs | join(', ') }}): {{ q.description }}{% if q.severity_values %}  severity: {{ q.severity_values | join(', ') }}{% endif %}{% if q.extent_values %}  extent: {{ q.extent_values | join(', ') }}{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}

# Schema: diagnosis values

The `diagnosis` field of each `diagnoses[]` record MUST match one of:
{% for d in schema.diagnoses %}
- `{{ d.name }}` ({{ d.organs | join(', ') }}): {{ d.description }}{% if d.synonyms %}  e.g. "{{ d.synonyms[0] }}"{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}

**H&E only; ignore special-stain quality issues.** Quality issues for OTHER stains (Gram, GMS, PAS, Trichrome, Iron, IHC) are NOT in scope and must NOT trigger `out_of_focus` / `inadequate_for_dx` / `not_performed` flags. The MORPHOLOGICAL RESULT of a special stain IS in scope (e.g. "GMS positive for fungal organisms" → `fungal` finding).

# Output format

Return a single JSON object (no comments, no extra keys, no text outside the JSON):

```
{
  "case_id": "<the case_id below>",
  "findings": [
    {
      "organ": "<one of the organs>",
      "text_source": "<one of: site_report, cpl_review_of_scans, cpl_slides, implicit_cpl>",
      "condition": "<schema condition name>",
      "severity": "<schema severity value or null>",
      "extent": "<schema extent value or null>",
      "modifiers": { "<modifier_key>": "<schema-allowed value>" },
      "supporting_quote": "<verbatim phrase ≤120 chars>"
    }
  ],
  "negations": [
    { "organ": "<organ>", "text_source": "<text_source>", "negation_group": "<negation_group>", "supporting_quote": "<verbatim>" }
  ],
  "quality_flags": [
    { "organ": "<organ>", "text_source": "<text_source>", "flag": "<flag>", "severity": null, "extent": null, "modifiers": {}, "supporting_quote": "<verbatim>" }
  ],
  "uncertain": [
    { "organ": "<organ>", "text_source": "<text_source>", "condition": "<schema condition name>", "reason": "<one of: hedge, material_unstated, pathologist_uncertainty>", "supporting_quote": "<verbatim>" }
  ],
  "diagnoses": [
    { "organ": "<organ>", "text_source": "<text_source>", "diagnosis": "<schema diagnosis name>", "supporting_quote": "<verbatim>" }
  ]
}
```

`modifiers` may be `{}`. `uncertain` and `diagnoses` may be `[]` (most cases have none). **Strict deduplication**: at most ONE record per `(organ, text_source, condition|negation_group|flag|diagnosis)` key. If no listed value fits a `severity`, `extent` or modifier field, set it to `null`. Never coin a value: a value that is not listed cannot be emitted.

The `uncertain[]` array records cases where the pathologist hedged a specific morphology; see Principle 12. An uncertain entry signals "neither emit as positive in `findings[]` NOR leave as a clean negative". The affected (case, organ, condition) label is masked downstream.

